# Breaks R-4 by asking for the one clause of it that has nothing behind it.
#
# R-4's third sentence says `@[Monomorphize]` forces specialisation across a
# module boundary. SPEC.md III.9 records what that is worth today: nothing in
# the compiler mentions the annotation, a dictionary or a GC shape. So this is
# not a feature that misbehaves, it is a name the compiler has never heard,
# and the rejection below is a compiler declining to accept a promise it
# cannot keep rather than compiling the program as though the rule were built.
#
# What runs instead of the dictionary is the rule's second sentence applied
# everywhere: a generic's body travels in the artifact and every consumer
# compiles it again for the types it uses. `bench/generic_boundary.py` is the
# measurement of what that costs a consumer's front end.
module diagnostics/r4_dictionary

@[Monomorphize]
pub def twice(x : T) : Array(T) forall T
  [x, x]
end

puts twice(1).size
